AB  - The availability of climate information is essential to support various sectors such as disaster mitigation, the agricultural sector, plantations, mining, and other strategic sectors. One of the important climate elements is rainfall. Because the information about rainfall is important, measurement at many points and continuously becomes a necessity. However, direct monitoring cannot be applied because of the limitation of funds and the equipment. One way to monitor rainfall occurrence is using satellite data; one uses Tropical Rainfall Measuring Mission (TRMM) data. This research aims to estimate the rainfall from TRMM data and evaluate the accuracy. The data was used in this research is monthly rainfall data from Pesawaran Meteorology and Geophysics Agency (BMKG Pesawaran) and monthly data from TRMM for 2000–2010. The results show that the R2 of the original TRMM and observation data is 0.6561 with RSME 123.19 mm. After applying Machine Learning with random forest fitting, the R2 was increased to 0.8876, and RSME decreased to 41.2 mm. The estimation data can be used as general information from these results, and the model estimation can be improved through machine learning.
